  "scientific_result": "R1.8 prospectively replicated the unchanged R1.7 R5 noncommuting-primitive null in an attempt-disjoint holdout (0/888 state-certified attempts) and established a state-certified phase-trajectory platform. The preregistered phase-distance algorithm-excess court also returned 0/888, but posthoc RAVEL showed that its null statistic was mismatched and over-conservative: frozen max-excursion-envelope thresholds exceeded the entire holdout candidate-reversal maximum in all 14 observed method×phase combinations. A posthoc matched-statistic remand recovered a 4.36% standardized attempt tail, but this was below the 5.96% leave-one-attempt-out calibration familywise null and therefore remained null-compatible. R1.8 does not identify cognitive recovery or cognitive error.",
